Public technical demonstration of the AKBASCORE MAM architecture on a third transformer model family. Mustafa Akbaş (AkbasCore AI Teknoloji) discovered and developed this numerical-memory mechanism (first public record: DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23245358, 8 October 2026; second model family: DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23257347, 9 October 2026); this DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat record is dated 10 October 2026.
A new numerical-memory paradigm for frozen language models.
Derived from MAMDSK-20261010-194411-0001-C00M_FULL_RUN_LOG_payload.json (SHA-256 6102e3cb88a35d4e331b00d9e15115c59d6478cb47fbe496633145905de4681f). Manifest: run_manifest_MAMDSK-20261010-194411-0001-C00M.json.
This is a LIVE run of the frozen DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat incremental MLA DC3 engine (596.py, unchanged). It is not TEST596; the TEST596 reference values are reproduced verbatim, never recomputed.
Cross-Model Replication — Third Model Family: DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat (MLA, DC3). After Mistral-7B (DC6) and Qwen2.5-7B (DC3), the AKBASCORE MAM architecture has been implemented on DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat, a model family with multi-head latent attention, using a model-specific consolidation boundary and the same write → init → append → ask cycle.
On the shared 72-question panel the DeepSeek result is 69/72; the three failed cases are reported in full.
Three model families are experimental evidence that the architecture transfers across models; they are not evidence that it works in every language model. Earlier records are cited as references only; every number in this demonstration comes from DeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat.
Earlier records (references only): AKBASCORE MAM v1.0 — Source-Free Persistent Memory for Frozen LLMs via DC6 Consolidation (Mistral-7B) · DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23245358 · https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23245358 · AKBASCORE MAM v1.1 — Cross-Model Replication: Source-Free Persistent Memory for Frozen LLMs on Qwen2.5-7B (DC3) · DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23257347 · https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23257347
